WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.000
This synthetic partial transcript starts in the middle of a longer video and intentionally marks the capture as incomplete.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:24.000
The quality gate should allow a dry run because there is useful text for review, but it must not import by default.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Operators need an explicit allow partial transcript flag before this material can become a durable knowledge base article.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:48.000
The flag does not mean the transcript is complete; it only records that a human accepted a partial source for a controlled case.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:01:00.000
The importer should still preserve metadata, language, transcript kind, character count, and a warning that review is required.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:12.000
If the transcript were shorter than the minimum threshold, the same flag would not be enough to create a knowledge base entry.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:24.000
This fixture therefore contains enough visible text to cross the import threshold while remaining clearly labeled as partial.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:36.000
It exercises the precise boundary between useful partial transcript material and weak metadata-only fallback text.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:48.000
The resulting report should say import is blocked without the flag and allowed with the flag, without changing web or WeChat routes.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:02:00.000
That behavior protects the knowledge base from thin video entries while keeping a deliberate escape hatch for reviewed partial transcripts.
